  "term": "social marketing",
  "definition": "Social marketing is the use of marketing methods to encourage ideas, attitudes, and behaviors that support a social goal. It focuses on increasing acceptance of beneficial practices in specific groups for the good of the audience and society rather than for the marketer’s gain.",
